-- title:
--   Stalk dominated by R₁ forces a non-closed point
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ with $5 \le p$ and a package $\mathfrak{X} : \mathtt{DRModelPackage}\ p$, which bundles properness, flatness and integrality of the structure morphism `DRModel.toBase p` of the two-chart integral model of the field $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldFull}\ p$ with coordinate $\mathtt{jFull}\ p$ over $\mathbb{Z}$, integral closedness of its sections on affine opens, curve models over $\mathbb{Q}$ and over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ identified with the corresponding base changes together with their Galois and place compatibilities, two cusp sections, and a smooth locus. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is $(p)$, with fraction field $K$ and a ring map $\iota_K : K \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and write $\mathfrak{X}_O$ for the fibre product of `DRModel.toBase p` with $\operatorname{Spec} O \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$, assumed integral. Let $x$ be a point of $\mathfrak{X}_O$ and $\varphi$ a ring homomorphism from the function field of $\mathfrak{X}_O$ to $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ (1 \cdot p)$, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series generated by the coefficientwise images of $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldFull}\ p$. Two normalisations are imposed: for $a \in O$, $\varphi$ sends the germ at $x$ of the global function pulled back from $a$ along the second projection to the constant $\iota_K(a)$; and, the preimage under the first projection of the finite chart being assumed non-empty, for every $a$ in the algebra of elements of $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldFull}\ p$ integral over $\mathbb{Z}[\mathtt{jFull}\ p]$, $\varphi$ carries the germ of $a$ on that open to the Laurent series $\mathtt{coeffEmb}$ of $a$. Further data: a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, an algebraically closed perfect field $k$ of characteristic $p$, a homomorphism $red : A \to k$, modular polynomial data for $p$ satisfying Kronecker's congruence, integrality of the two Hecke degeneracy embeddings at level $1$ and $p$, a place specialisation $P$ in these data, a prolongation tuple $R$ over $P$ with its two regular prolongations $R_1, R_2$, the inclusion $\iota_K(O) \subseteq A$, and a homomorphism $toκ : O \to k$ agreeing with $red \circ \iota_K$. Finally let $c$ be a point of $\mathfrak{X}_O$ lying over the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} O$ such that $\varphi$ maps the image in the function field of the whole stalk at $c$ into the valuation ring $R_1.\mathtt{integers}$, and maps the image of the maximal ideal of that stalk into the non-units of $R_1.\mathtt{integers}$. Then the singleton $\{c\}$ is not closed in $\mathfrak{X}_O$.
--
--   This is the first of the two Gauss-ring halves of the branch-identification step: a point of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model over $O$ whose local ring is dominated, through the chosen identification $\varphi$ of function fields, by the first prolongation ring $R_1$ cannot be a closed point, hence is the generic point of a component of the special fibre. The domination hypothesis on the maximal ideal is what rules out closed points, since at a closed point the chart coordinate $j$ satisfies a monic equation over $O$ whose value would then be a non-unit. It is used in [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.mem_integers_and_mem_integers_of_stalk_of_specializes`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.mem_integers_and_mem_integers_of_stalk_of_specializes).
